* ADG5248F Analog Multiplexer Test

* Include Analog Devices library
.lib ADI.lib

* Power Supplies (+/- 15V)
Vdd VDD 0 15
Vss VSS 0 -15

* Logic Enable (5V)
Ven EN 0 5

* Address lines to select Channel 1 (A2=0, A1=0, A0=0)
Va0 A0 0 0
Va1 A1 0 0
Va2 A2 0 0

* Primary Input Signal on Channel 1 (1 kHz, 500 mV amplitude sine)
Vin IN 0 SINE(0 0.5 1k)

* ADG5248F Subcircuit Instantiation
* Typical ADI Multiplexer Pinout: S1 S2 S3 S4 S5 S6 S7 S8 D A0 A1 A2 EN VDD VSS GND SF
X1 IN 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 OUT A0 A1 A2 EN VDD VSS 0 SF ADG5248F

* Pull-up resistor for Source Fault (SF) open-drain output
Rsf SF EN 10k

* Output Load
Rload OUT 0 1Meg

* Transient Analysis for 10ms (10 cycles at 1kHz)
.tran 0 10m 0 1u

* Measurements to calculate gain in dB
.meas tran max_in MAX V(IN) from=2m to=10m
.meas tran max_out MAX V(OUT) from=2m to=10m
.meas tran gain_db PARAM 20*log10(max_out/max_in)

.end
